[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":1831},["ShallowReactive",2],{"page-\u002Fpython\u002F01-introduction-and-setup":3},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":317,"extension":1825,"meta":1826,"navigation":352,"path":1827,"seo":1828,"stem":1829,"__hash__":1830},"content\u002Fpython\u002F01-introduction-and-setup.md","01 — Introduction & Setup",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":1801},"minimark",[9,13,18,27,112,119,123,135,233,239,244,263,267,301,305,308,508,552,556,566,570,577,588,695,699,706,728,834,838,858,926,930,954,977,986,989,1027,1104,1181,1184,1232,1236,1299,1302,1306,1410,1414,1499,1503,1616,1620,1627,1686,1757,1761,1797],[10,11,5],"h1",{"id":12},"_01-introduction-setup",[14,15,17],"h2",{"id":16},"what-is-python","What Is Python?",[19,20,21,22,26],"p",{},"Python is a ",[23,24,25],"strong",{},"high-level, dynamically typed, multi-paradigm"," language created by Guido van Rossum, first released in 1991. Key characteristics:",[28,29,30,37,52,66,92,106],"ul",{},[31,32,33,36],"li",{},[23,34,35],{},"Dynamic typing"," — variables are names bound to objects; a name can be rebound to a value of any type at runtime.",[31,38,39,42,43,47,48,51],{},[23,40,41],{},"Interpreted, but compiled to bytecode"," — source (",[44,45,46],"code",{},".py",") is compiled to bytecode (",[44,49,50],{},".pyc",") which runs on a virtual machine (the CPython VM). It is not \"purely interpreted\" line-by-line, nor is it compiled to native machine code ahead of time like C or Rust.",[31,53,54,57,58,61,62,65],{},[23,55,56],{},"Multi-paradigm"," — supports procedural, object-oriented (everything is an object), and functional styles (first-class functions, closures, ",[44,59,60],{},"map","\u002F",[44,63,64],{},"filter",").",[31,67,68,71,72,75,76,75,79,75,82,75,85,75,88,91],{},[23,69,70],{},"Batteries included"," — a large standard library (",[44,73,74],{},"os",", ",[44,77,78],{},"json",[44,80,81],{},"datetime",[44,83,84],{},"collections",[44,86,87],{},"itertools",[44,89,90],{},"asyncio",", and more) ships with every installation.",[31,93,94,97,98,105],{},[23,95,96],{},"Readable by design"," — enforced significant whitespace (indentation defines blocks) and a philosophy captured in ",[99,100,104],"a",{"href":101,"rel":102},"https:\u002F\u002Fpeps.python.org\u002Fpep-0020\u002F",[103],"nofollow","PEP 20 — The Zen of Python",": \"There should be one — and preferably only one — obvious way to do it.\"",[31,107,108,111],{},[23,109,110],{},"Reference-counted with cycle-detecting GC"," — objects are freed via reference counting; a generational garbage collector handles reference cycles.",[19,113,114,115,118],{},"Run ",[44,116,117],{},"import this"," in any Python REPL to print the Zen of Python — it's an actual Easter egg module, not just a saying.",[14,120,122],{"id":121},"cpython-vs-other-implementations","CPython vs Other Implementations",[19,124,125,126,130,131,134],{},"\"Python\" is a ",[127,128,129],"em",{},"language specification","; there are multiple ",[127,132,133],{},"implementations"," that run it.",[136,137,138,154],"table",{},[139,140,141],"thead",{},[142,143,144,148,151],"tr",{},[145,146,147],"th",{},"Implementation",[145,149,150],{},"Description",[145,152,153],{},"When to use",[155,156,157,181,194,207,220],"tbody",{},[142,158,159,165,178],{},[160,161,162],"td",{},[23,163,164],{},"CPython",[160,166,167,168,75,171,75,174,177],{},"The reference implementation, written in C. What you get from python.org, ",[44,169,170],{},"pyenv",[44,172,173],{},"apt",[44,175,176],{},"brew",".",[160,179,180],{},"Default choice for almost everything.",[142,182,183,188,191],{},[160,184,185],{},[23,186,187],{},"PyPy",[160,189,190],{},"A Python implementation with a JIT (just-in-time) compiler, written in RPython. Often 4–10x faster for long-running, CPU-bound pure-Python code.",[160,192,193],{},"Long-running numeric\u002Falgorithmic workloads without heavy C-extension dependencies.",[142,195,196,201,204],{},[160,197,198],{},[23,199,200],{},"Jython",[160,202,203],{},"Runs on the JVM, compiles to Java bytecode. Largely inactive\u002Flegacy.",[160,205,206],{},"Interop with existing JVM codebases (rare today).",[142,208,209,214,217],{},[160,210,211],{},[23,212,213],{},"IronPython",[160,215,216],{},"Runs on .NET\u002FCLR.",[160,218,219],{},"Interop with .NET codebases.",[142,221,222,227,230],{},[160,223,224],{},[23,225,226],{},"MicroPython",[160,228,229],{},"A lean reimplementation for microcontrollers.",[160,231,232],{},"Embedded systems (ESP32, Raspberry Pi Pico).",[19,234,235,236,238],{},"Unless you have a specific reason (JIT speed, embedded target, VM interop), you want ",[23,237,164],{},". This curriculum assumes CPython 3.11+.",[240,241,243],"h3",{"id":242},"why-the-gil-matters-even-at-this-stage","Why \"the GIL\" matters even at this stage",[19,245,246,247,250,251,254,255,258,259,262],{},"CPython has a ",[23,248,249],{},"Global Interpreter Lock (GIL)"," — only one thread executes Python bytecode at a time, even on multi-core machines. This shapes idiomatic Python: CPU-bound parallelism uses ",[44,252,253],{},"multiprocessing"," (separate processes, no shared GIL) rather than ",[44,256,257],{},"threading",". Chapter 21 covers this in depth — mentioned here because it explains ",[127,260,261],{},"why"," Python's concurrency story looks different from Java's or Go's from day one.",[14,264,266],{"id":265},"python-2-vs-python-3","Python 2 vs Python 3",[19,268,269,270,273,274,277,278,281,282,285,286,289,290,292,293,296,297,300],{},"Python 2 reached end-of-life on ",[23,271,272],{},"January 1, 2020",". Every example in this curriculum targets ",[23,275,276],{},"Python 3.11+",". If you encounter Python 2 code (",[44,279,280],{},"print \"hello\""," without parentheses, ",[44,283,284],{},"xrange",", implicit integer division truncation being the ",[127,287,288],{},"default"," for ",[44,291,61],{},"), treat it as legacy and port it — the ",[44,294,295],{},"2to3"," tool and ",[44,298,299],{},"six"," compatibility shims exist but are rarely needed for new work in 2026.",[14,302,304],{"id":303},"installing-python-with-pyenv","Installing Python with pyenv",[19,306,307],{},"Never rely on your OS's system Python for development — on macOS and Linux it's often outdated, used internally by the OS itself, and modifying it can break system tools. Use a version manager.",[309,310,312],"code-wrapper",{"language":311},"bash",[313,314,318],"pre",{"className":315,"code":316,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","# macOS \u002F Linux — install pyenv\ncurl https:\u002F\u002Fpyenv.run | bash\n\n# Add to your shell profile (~\u002F.zshrc or ~\u002F.bashrc)\nexport PYENV_ROOT=\"$HOME\u002F.pyenv\"\nexport PATH=\"$PYENV_ROOT\u002Fbin:$PATH\"\neval \"$(pyenv init -)\"\n\n# Restart your shell, then:\npyenv install --list | grep \" 3.12\"   # see available 3.12.x versions\npyenv install 3.12.4\npyenv global 3.12.4                   # set as the default for your user\n\n# Per-project version (writes a .python-version file)\ncd my-project\npyenv local 3.12.4\n","",[44,319,320,329,347,354,360,382,406,421,426,432,454,464,478,483,489,498],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,322,325],"span",{"class":323,"line":324},"line",1,[321,326,328],{"class":327},"sdCPZ","# macOS \u002F Linux — install pyenv\n",[321,330,332,336,340,344],{"class":323,"line":331},2,[321,333,335],{"class":334},"sIsaT","curl",[321,337,339],{"class":338},"sJ6F3"," https:\u002F\u002Fpyenv.run",[321,341,343],{"class":342},"svdQ7"," |",[321,345,346],{"class":334}," bash\n",[321,348,350],{"class":323,"line":349},3,[321,351,353],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":352},true,"\n",[321,355,357],{"class":323,"line":356},4,[321,358,359],{"class":327},"# Add to your shell profile (~\u002F.zshrc or ~\u002F.bashrc)\n",[321,361,363,366,370,373,376,379],{"class":323,"line":362},5,[321,364,365],{"class":342},"export",[321,367,369],{"class":368},"ssxIu"," PYENV_ROOT",[321,371,372],{"class":342},"=",[321,374,375],{"class":338},"\"",[321,377,378],{"class":368},"$HOME",[321,380,381],{"class":338},"\u002F.pyenv\"\n",[321,383,385,387,390,392,394,397,400,403],{"class":323,"line":384},6,[321,386,365],{"class":342},[321,388,389],{"class":368}," PATH",[321,391,372],{"class":342},[321,393,375],{"class":338},[321,395,396],{"class":368},"$PYENV_ROOT",[321,398,399],{"class":338},"\u002Fbin:",[321,401,402],{"class":368},"$PATH",[321,404,405],{"class":338},"\"\n",[321,407,409,413,416,418],{"class":323,"line":408},7,[321,410,412],{"class":411},"snvgF","eval",[321,414,415],{"class":338}," \"$(",[321,417,170],{"class":334},[321,419,420],{"class":338}," init -)\"\n",[321,422,424],{"class":323,"line":423},8,[321,425,353],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":352},[321,427,429],{"class":323,"line":428},9,[321,430,431],{"class":327},"# Restart your shell, then:\n",[321,433,435,437,440,443,445,448,451],{"class":323,"line":434},10,[321,436,170],{"class":334},[321,438,439],{"class":338}," install",[321,441,442],{"class":411}," --list",[321,444,343],{"class":342},[321,446,447],{"class":334}," grep",[321,449,450],{"class":338}," \" 3.12\"",[321,452,453],{"class":327},"   # see available 3.12.x versions\n",[321,455,457,459,461],{"class":323,"line":456},11,[321,458,170],{"class":334},[321,460,439],{"class":338},[321,462,463],{"class":411}," 3.12.4\n",[321,465,467,469,472,475],{"class":323,"line":466},12,[321,468,170],{"class":334},[321,470,471],{"class":338}," global",[321,473,474],{"class":411}," 3.12.4",[321,476,477],{"class":327},"                   # set as the default for your user\n",[321,479,481],{"class":323,"line":480},13,[321,482,353],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":352},[321,484,486],{"class":323,"line":485},14,[321,487,488],{"class":327},"# Per-project version (writes a .python-version file)\n",[321,490,492,495],{"class":323,"line":491},15,[321,493,494],{"class":411},"cd",[321,496,497],{"class":338}," my-project\n",[321,499,501,503,506],{"class":323,"line":500},16,[321,502,170],{"class":334},[321,504,505],{"class":338}," local",[321,507,463],{"class":411},[309,509,510],{"language":311},[313,511,513],{"className":315,"code":512,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"# Verify\npython --version    # Python 3.12.4\npython3 --version   # same, on systems where \"python\" still points elsewhere\nwhich python         # confirm it resolves inside ~\u002F.pyenv\u002Fshims\n",[44,514,515,520,531,541],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,516,517],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,518,519],{"class":327},"# Verify\n",[321,521,522,525,528],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,523,524],{"class":334},"python",[321,526,527],{"class":411}," --version",[321,529,530],{"class":327},"    # Python 3.12.4\n",[321,532,533,536,538],{"class":323,"line":349},[321,534,535],{"class":334},"python3",[321,537,527],{"class":411},[321,539,540],{"class":327},"   # same, on systems where \"python\" still points elsewhere\n",[321,542,543,546,549],{"class":323,"line":356},[321,544,545],{"class":411},"which",[321,547,548],{"class":338}," python",[321,550,551],{"class":327},"         # confirm it resolves inside ~\u002F.pyenv\u002Fshims\n",[240,553,555],{"id":554},"windows","Windows",[19,557,558,559,562,563,565],{},"Use the official installer from python.org (check \"Add python.exe to PATH\"), or ",[44,560,561],{},"pyenv-win",", or the Microsoft Store package for quick starts. For serious development, ",[44,564,561],{}," mirrors the Unix workflow above.",[14,567,569],{"id":568},"the-repl","The REPL",[19,571,572,573,576],{},"Python ships an interactive ",[23,574,575],{},"Read-Eval-Print Loop",". It's invaluable for exploring APIs, testing snippets, and debugging.",[309,578,579],{"language":311},[313,580,582],{"className":315,"code":581,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"python\n",[44,583,584],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,585,586],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,587,581],{"class":334},[309,589,590],{"language":524},[313,591,594],{"className":592,"code":593,"language":524,"meta":317,"style":317},"language-python shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark",">>> 2 + 2\n4\n>>> import math\n>>> math.sqrt(16)\n4.0\n>>> name = \"Ada\"\n>>> f\"Hello, {name}!\"\n'Hello, Ada!'\n>>> exit()   # or Ctrl+D\n",[44,595,596,610,615,625,638,643,655,677,682],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,597,598,601,604,607],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,599,600],{"class":342},">>>",[321,602,603],{"class":411}," 2",[321,605,606],{"class":342}," +",[321,608,609],{"class":411}," 2\n",[321,611,612],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,613,614],{"class":411},"4\n",[321,616,617,619,622],{"class":323,"line":349},[321,618,600],{"class":342},[321,620,621],{"class":342}," import",[321,623,624],{"class":368}," math\n",[321,626,627,629,632,635],{"class":323,"line":356},[321,628,600],{"class":342},[321,630,631],{"class":368}," math.sqrt(",[321,633,634],{"class":411},"16",[321,636,637],{"class":368},")\n",[321,639,640],{"class":323,"line":362},[321,641,642],{"class":411},"4.0\n",[321,644,645,647,650,652],{"class":323,"line":384},[321,646,600],{"class":342},[321,648,649],{"class":368}," name ",[321,651,372],{"class":342},[321,653,654],{"class":338}," \"Ada\"\n",[321,656,657,659,662,665,668,671,674],{"class":323,"line":408},[321,658,600],{"class":342},[321,660,661],{"class":342}," f",[321,663,664],{"class":338},"\"Hello, ",[321,666,667],{"class":411},"{",[321,669,670],{"class":368},"name",[321,672,673],{"class":411},"}",[321,675,676],{"class":338},"!\"\n",[321,678,679],{"class":323,"line":423},[321,680,681],{"class":338},"'Hello, Ada!'\n",[321,683,684,686,689,692],{"class":323,"line":428},[321,685,600],{"class":342},[321,687,688],{"class":411}," exit",[321,690,691],{"class":368},"()   ",[321,693,694],{"class":327},"# or Ctrl+D\n",[240,696,698],{"id":697},"ipython-a-vastly-better-repl","IPython — a vastly better REPL",[19,700,701,702,705],{},"The stock REPL is minimal. ",[44,703,704],{},"ipython"," adds syntax highlighting, tab completion, magic commands, and better tracebacks.",[309,707,708],{"language":311},[313,709,711],{"className":315,"code":710,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"pip install ipython\nipython\n",[44,712,713,723],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,714,715,718,720],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,716,717],{"class":334},"pip",[321,719,439],{"class":338},[321,721,722],{"class":338}," ipython\n",[321,724,725],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,726,727],{"class":334},"ipython\n",[309,729,730],{"language":524},[313,731,733],{"className":592,"code":732,"language":524,"meta":317,"style":317},"In [1]: %timeit sum(range(1000))\n6.53 µs ± 45.1 ns per loop (mean ± std. dev. of 7 runs, 100000 loops each)\n\nIn [2]: import requests   # tab-completion, ? for docs\nIn [3]: requests.get?     # shows docstring and signature\n",[44,734,735,769,795,799,817],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,736,737,740,743,746,749,752,755,758,761,763,766],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,738,739],{"class":368},"In [",[321,741,742],{"class":411},"1",[321,744,745],{"class":368},"]: ",[321,747,748],{"class":342},"%",[321,750,751],{"class":368},"timeit ",[321,753,754],{"class":411},"sum",[321,756,757],{"class":368},"(",[321,759,760],{"class":411},"range",[321,762,757],{"class":368},[321,764,765],{"class":411},"1000",[321,767,768],{"class":368},"))\n",[321,770,771,774,777,780,783,786,789,792],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,772,773],{"class":411},"6.53",[321,775,776],{"class":368}," µs ± ",[321,778,779],{"class":411},"45.1",[321,781,782],{"class":368}," ns per loop (mean ± std. dev. of ",[321,784,785],{"class":411},"7",[321,787,788],{"class":368}," runs, ",[321,790,791],{"class":411},"100000",[321,793,794],{"class":368}," loops each)\n",[321,796,797],{"class":323,"line":349},[321,798,353],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":352},[321,800,801,803,806,808,811,814],{"class":323,"line":356},[321,802,739],{"class":368},[321,804,805],{"class":411},"2",[321,807,745],{"class":368},[321,809,810],{"class":342},"import",[321,812,813],{"class":368}," requests   ",[321,815,816],{"class":327},"# tab-completion, ? for docs\n",[321,818,819,821,824,827,831],{"class":323,"line":362},[321,820,739],{"class":368},[321,822,823],{"class":411},"3",[321,825,826],{"class":368},"]: requests.get",[321,828,830],{"class":829},"sMKGj","?",[321,832,833],{"class":327},"     # shows docstring and signature\n",[14,835,837],{"id":836},"running-scripts","Running Scripts",[309,839,841],{"language":524,"filename":840},"hello.py",[313,842,844],{"className":592,"code":843,"language":524,"meta":317,"style":317},"print(\"Hello, World!\")\n",[44,845,846],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,847,848,851,853,856],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,849,850],{"class":411},"print",[321,852,757],{"class":368},[321,854,855],{"class":338},"\"Hello, World!\"",[321,857,637],{"class":368},[309,859,860],{"language":311},[313,861,863],{"className":315,"code":862,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"python hello.py\n# Hello, World!\n\n# Run as a module (adds the script's directory to sys.path differently —\n# matters for relative imports, see chapter 17)\npython -m hello\n\n# Pass arguments\npython hello.py arg1 arg2   # available via sys.argv\n",[44,864,865,872,877,881,886,891,901,905,910],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,866,867,869],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,868,524],{"class":334},[321,870,871],{"class":338}," hello.py\n",[321,873,874],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,875,876],{"class":327},"# Hello, World!\n",[321,878,879],{"class":323,"line":349},[321,880,353],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":352},[321,882,883],{"class":323,"line":356},[321,884,885],{"class":327},"# Run as a module (adds the script's directory to sys.path differently —\n",[321,887,888],{"class":323,"line":362},[321,889,890],{"class":327},"# matters for relative imports, see chapter 17)\n",[321,892,893,895,898],{"class":323,"line":384},[321,894,524],{"class":334},[321,896,897],{"class":411}," -m",[321,899,900],{"class":338}," hello\n",[321,902,903],{"class":323,"line":408},[321,904,353],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":352},[321,906,907],{"class":323,"line":423},[321,908,909],{"class":327},"# Pass arguments\n",[321,911,912,914,917,920,923],{"class":323,"line":428},[321,913,524],{"class":334},[321,915,916],{"class":338}," hello.py",[321,918,919],{"class":338}," arg1",[321,921,922],{"class":338}," arg2",[321,924,925],{"class":327},"   # available via sys.argv\n",[240,927,929],{"id":928},"the-shebang-line-and-executable-scripts","The shebang line and executable scripts",[309,931,933],{"language":524,"filename":932},"greet.py",[313,934,936],{"className":592,"code":935,"language":524,"meta":317,"style":317},"#!\u002Fusr\u002Fbin\u002Fenv python3\nprint(\"Hello from an executable script!\")\n",[44,937,938,943],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,939,940],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,941,942],{"class":327},"#!\u002Fusr\u002Fbin\u002Fenv python3\n",[321,944,945,947,949,952],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,946,850],{"class":411},[321,948,757],{"class":368},[321,950,951],{"class":338},"\"Hello from an executable script!\"",[321,953,637],{"class":368},[309,955,956],{"language":311},[313,957,959],{"className":315,"code":958,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"chmod +x greet.py\n.\u002Fgreet.py\n",[44,960,961,972],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,962,963,966,969],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,964,965],{"class":334},"chmod",[321,967,968],{"class":338}," +x",[321,970,971],{"class":338}," greet.py\n",[321,973,974],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,975,976],{"class":334},".\u002Fgreet.py\n",[14,978,980,982,983,985],{"id":979},"py-vs-pyc-what-actually-happens-when-you-run-python",[44,981,46],{}," vs ",[44,984,50],{}," — What Actually Happens When You Run Python",[19,987,988],{},"A common misconception is that Python is \"purely interpreted.\" In reality:",[990,991,992,1006,1020],"ol",{},[31,993,994,995,998,999,1001,1002,1005],{},"CPython ",[23,996,997],{},"compiles"," your ",[44,1000,46],{}," source into ",[23,1003,1004],{},"bytecode"," (an intermediate, platform-independent instruction set for the CPython VM).",[31,1007,1008,1009,1012,1013,1015,1016,1019],{},"That bytecode is cached in a ",[44,1010,1011],{},"__pycache__\u002F"," directory as ",[44,1014,50],{}," files, named like ",[44,1017,1018],{},"module.cpython-312.pyc",", so re-running unchanged modules skips re-compilation.",[31,1021,1022,1023,1026],{},"The ",[23,1024,1025],{},"CPython VM"," then interprets that bytecode — this step is the actual \"interpretation.\"",[309,1028,1029],{"language":311},[313,1030,1032],{"className":315,"code":1031,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"# Force-see the bytecode cache\npython -c \"import mymodule\"\nls __pycache__\u002F\n# mymodule.cpython-312.pyc\n\n# Inspect bytecode directly\npython -c \"\nimport dis\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b\ndis.dis(add)\n\"\n",[44,1033,1034,1039,1049,1057,1062,1066,1071,1080,1085,1090,1095,1100],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,1035,1036],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,1037,1038],{"class":327},"# Force-see the bytecode cache\n",[321,1040,1041,1043,1046],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,1042,524],{"class":334},[321,1044,1045],{"class":411}," -c",[321,1047,1048],{"class":338}," \"import mymodule\"\n",[321,1050,1051,1054],{"class":323,"line":349},[321,1052,1053],{"class":334},"ls",[321,1055,1056],{"class":338}," __pycache__\u002F\n",[321,1058,1059],{"class":323,"line":356},[321,1060,1061],{"class":327},"# mymodule.cpython-312.pyc\n",[321,1063,1064],{"class":323,"line":362},[321,1065,353],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":352},[321,1067,1068],{"class":323,"line":384},[321,1069,1070],{"class":327},"# Inspect bytecode directly\n",[321,1072,1073,1075,1077],{"class":323,"line":408},[321,1074,524],{"class":334},[321,1076,1045],{"class":411},[321,1078,1079],{"class":338}," \"\n",[321,1081,1082],{"class":323,"line":423},[321,1083,1084],{"class":338},"import dis\n",[321,1086,1087],{"class":323,"line":428},[321,1088,1089],{"class":338},"def add(a, b):\n",[321,1091,1092],{"class":323,"line":434},[321,1093,1094],{"class":338},"    return a + b\n",[321,1096,1097],{"class":323,"line":456},[321,1098,1099],{"class":338},"dis.dis(add)\n",[321,1101,1102],{"class":323,"line":466},[321,1103,405],{"class":338},[309,1105,1106],{"language":524},[313,1107,1109],{"className":592,"code":1108,"language":524,"meta":317,"style":317},"  2           0 RESUME                   0\n  3           2 LOAD_FAST                0 (a)\n              4 LOAD_FAST                1 (b)\n              6 BINARY_OP                0 (+)\n             10 RETURN_VALUE\n",[44,1110,1111,1125,1142,1155,1173],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,1112,1113,1116,1119,1122],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,1114,1115],{"class":411},"  2",[321,1117,1118],{"class":411},"           0",[321,1120,1121],{"class":411}," RESUME",[321,1123,1124],{"class":411},"                   0\n",[321,1126,1127,1130,1133,1136,1139],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,1128,1129],{"class":411},"  3",[321,1131,1132],{"class":411},"           2",[321,1134,1135],{"class":411}," LOAD_FAST",[321,1137,1138],{"class":411},"                0",[321,1140,1141],{"class":368}," (a)\n",[321,1143,1144,1147,1149,1152],{"class":323,"line":349},[321,1145,1146],{"class":411},"              4",[321,1148,1135],{"class":411},[321,1150,1151],{"class":411},"                1",[321,1153,1154],{"class":368}," (b)\n",[321,1156,1157,1160,1163,1165,1168,1171],{"class":323,"line":356},[321,1158,1159],{"class":411},"              6",[321,1161,1162],{"class":411}," BINARY_OP",[321,1164,1138],{"class":411},[321,1166,1167],{"class":368}," (",[321,1169,1170],{"class":342},"+",[321,1172,637],{"class":368},[321,1174,1175,1178],{"class":323,"line":362},[321,1176,1177],{"class":411},"             10",[321,1179,1180],{"class":411}," RETURN_VALUE\n",[19,1182,1183],{},"This matters because:",[28,1185,1186,1194,1211],{},[31,1187,1188,1190,1191,1193],{},[44,1189,50],{}," caching is ",[127,1192,261],{}," the second run of an unchanged script\u002Fmodule import is faster than the first.",[31,1195,1196,1198,1199,1202,1203,1206,1207,1210],{},[44,1197,50],{}," files are ",[23,1200,1201],{},"not"," portable across major\u002Fminor Python versions or CPU architectures in a meaningful \"compiled binary\" sense — they're not a substitute for ahead-of-time compilation like C's ",[44,1204,1205],{},".o"," files. They only skip the ",[127,1208,1209],{},"parse+compile"," step, not execution.",[31,1212,1213,1214,1217,1218,1220,1221,1223,1224,1227,1228,1231],{},"Top-level script files (the one you invoke with ",[44,1215,1216],{},"python script.py",") are ",[23,1219,1201],{}," cached to ",[44,1222,50],{}," — only ",[127,1225,1226],{},"imported"," modules are. This is a frequent point of confusion when people expect ",[44,1229,1230],{},"__pycache__"," to appear next to their entry-point script.",[14,1233,1235],{"id":1234},"interpreted-vs-compiled-where-python-actually-sits","Interpreted vs Compiled — Where Python Actually Sits",[136,1237,1238,1253],{},[139,1239,1240],{},[142,1241,1242,1244,1247,1250],{},[145,1243],{},[145,1245,1246],{},"C \u002F Rust",[145,1248,1249],{},"Java \u002F C#",[145,1251,1252],{},"Python (CPython)",[155,1254,1255,1269,1283],{},[142,1256,1257,1260,1263,1266],{},[160,1258,1259],{},"Compiles to",[160,1261,1262],{},"Native machine code (ahead of time)",[160,1264,1265],{},"Bytecode (ahead of time), JIT to native at runtime",[160,1267,1268],{},"Bytecode (lazily, on import\u002Ffirst run)",[142,1270,1271,1274,1277,1280],{},[160,1272,1273],{},"Execution",[160,1275,1276],{},"Direct CPU execution",[160,1278,1279],{},"JVM\u002FCLR interprets or JIT-compiles bytecode",[160,1281,1282],{},"CPython VM interprets bytecode (no JIT by default)",[142,1284,1285,1288,1291,1293],{},[160,1286,1287],{},"Type checking",[160,1289,1290],{},"Compile-time (static)",[160,1292,1290],{},[160,1294,1295,1296],{},"Runtime (dynamic) — see chapter 20 for optional static checking via ",[44,1297,1298],{},"mypy",[19,1300,1301],{},"Python's lack of a default JIT is precisely why CPU-bound pure-Python loops are slow compared to Java\u002FC#\u002FRust — and why performance-critical Python code either delegates to C extensions (numpy, pandas — see chapter 26) or reaches for PyPy.",[14,1303,1305],{"id":1304},"project-structure-conventions","Project Structure Conventions",[309,1307,1308],{"language":311},[313,1309,1311],{"className":315,"code":1310,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"my-project\u002F\n├── pyproject.toml       # modern project metadata, deps, build config (ch. 25)\n├── README.md\n├── src\u002F\n│   └── my_project\u002F\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── main.py\n│       └── utils.py\n├── tests\u002F\n│   └── test_utils.py\n└── .python-version      # pyenv local version pin\n",[44,1312,1313,1318,1329,1336,1343,1354,1364,1373,1383,1390,1399],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,1314,1315],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,1316,1317],{"class":334},"my-project\u002F\n",[321,1319,1320,1323,1326],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,1321,1322],{"class":334},"├──",[321,1324,1325],{"class":338}," pyproject.toml",[321,1327,1328],{"class":327},"       # modern project metadata, deps, build config (ch. 25)\n",[321,1330,1331,1333],{"class":323,"line":349},[321,1332,1322],{"class":334},[321,1334,1335],{"class":338}," README.md\n",[321,1337,1338,1340],{"class":323,"line":356},[321,1339,1322],{"class":334},[321,1341,1342],{"class":338}," src\u002F\n",[321,1344,1345,1348,1351],{"class":323,"line":362},[321,1346,1347],{"class":334},"│",[321,1349,1350],{"class":338},"   └──",[321,1352,1353],{"class":338}," my_project\u002F\n",[321,1355,1356,1358,1361],{"class":323,"line":384},[321,1357,1347],{"class":334},[321,1359,1360],{"class":338},"       ├──",[321,1362,1363],{"class":338}," __init__.py\n",[321,1365,1366,1368,1370],{"class":323,"line":408},[321,1367,1347],{"class":334},[321,1369,1360],{"class":338},[321,1371,1372],{"class":338}," main.py\n",[321,1374,1375,1377,1380],{"class":323,"line":423},[321,1376,1347],{"class":334},[321,1378,1379],{"class":338},"       └──",[321,1381,1382],{"class":338}," utils.py\n",[321,1384,1385,1387],{"class":323,"line":428},[321,1386,1322],{"class":334},[321,1388,1389],{"class":338}," tests\u002F\n",[321,1391,1392,1394,1396],{"class":323,"line":434},[321,1393,1347],{"class":334},[321,1395,1350],{"class":338},[321,1397,1398],{"class":338}," test_utils.py\n",[321,1400,1401,1404,1407],{"class":323,"line":456},[321,1402,1403],{"class":334},"└──",[321,1405,1406],{"class":338}," .python-version",[321,1408,1409],{"class":327},"      # pyenv local version pin\n",[14,1411,1413],{"id":1412},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[28,1415,1416,1428,1453,1476,1488],{},[31,1417,1418,1423,1424,1427],{},[23,1419,1420],{},[44,1421,1422],{},"python -i script.py"," — Debug: runs the script, then drops you into a REPL with all its top-level names still bound, so you can poke at final state without adding ",[44,1425,1426],{},"breakpoint()"," calls.",[31,1429,1430,1436,1437,1440,1441,1444,1445,1448,1449,1452],{},[23,1431,1432,1435],{},[44,1433,1434],{},"python -m"," runs installed tools as modules"," — ",[44,1438,1439],{},"python -m http.server 8000"," starts a static file server instantly; ",[44,1442,1443],{},"python -m venv .venv"," creates a virtual environment; ",[44,1446,1447],{},"python -m pip"," guarantees you're using the pip tied to ",[127,1450,1451],{},"this"," interpreter, sidestepping PATH ambiguity between multiple Pythons.",[31,1454,1455,1460,1461,1463,1464,1467,1468,1471,1472,1475],{},[23,1456,1457,1459],{},[44,1458,1426],{}," is the built-in debugger entry point"," — Since 3.7, calling ",[44,1462,1426],{}," anywhere in code drops into ",[44,1465,1466],{},"pdb"," (or whatever ",[44,1469,1470],{},"PYTHONBREAKPOINT"," points to) at that exact line — no ",[44,1473,1474],{},"import pdb; pdb.set_trace()"," boilerplate needed.",[31,1477,1478,1436,1484,1487],{},[23,1479,1480,1483],{},[44,1481,1482],{},"python -c"," for one-liners",[44,1485,1486],{},"python -c \"import platform; print(platform.python_version())\""," runs code without creating a file; useful in shell scripts and CI checks.",[31,1489,1490,1498],{},[23,1491,1492,1494,1495,1497],{},[44,1493,1230],{}," and ",[44,1496,50],{}," files are safe to delete"," — They're purely a compile cache; deleting them just forces recompilation on next import, never a correctness issue (unless you're debugging a Python-version bytecode mismatch bug).",[14,1500,1502],{"id":1501},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[28,1504,1505,1529,1546,1567,1585],{},[31,1506,1507,1513,1514,1516,1517,1519,1520,61,1522,1525,1526,1528],{},[23,1508,1509,982,1511],{},[44,1510,524],{},[44,1512,535],{}," — On many Linux distributions and older macOS versions, ",[44,1515,524],{}," either doesn't exist or still points to Python 2. Always use ",[44,1518,535],{}," explicitly in portable scripts, or better, use ",[44,1521,170],{},[44,1523,1524],{},"uv"," so ",[44,1527,524],{}," unambiguously resolves to your intended version.",[31,1530,1531,1536,1537,1539,1540,1542,1543,177],{},[23,1532,1533,1535],{},[44,1534,50],{}," files can go stale across environments"," — If you copy a ",[44,1538,1230],{}," directory between machines running different Python patch versions, CPython detects the mismatch via an embedded magic number and simply recompiles — it does not silently run incompatible bytecode. Still, don't commit ",[44,1541,1011],{}," to version control; add it to ",[44,1544,1545],{},".gitignore",[31,1547,1548,1436,1555,1558,1559,1562,1563,1566],{},[23,1549,1550,1551,1554],{},"The REPL's ",[44,1552,1553],{},"_"," holds the last expression's value",[44,1556,1557],{},">>> 2 + 2"," then ",[44,1560,1561],{},">>> _ * 10"," gives ",[44,1564,1565],{},"40",". This is genuinely useful but invisible unless you know it exists, and it only works for expressions typed directly at the prompt, not inside scripts.",[31,1568,1569,1580,1581,1584],{},[23,1570,1571,1572,1575,1576,1579],{},"Indentation errors are ",[44,1573,1574],{},"IndentationError",", not ",[44,1577,1578],{},"SyntaxError",", and mixing tabs\u002Fspaces is a runtime error, not a style nit"," — Python 3 raises ",[44,1582,1583],{},"TabError: inconsistent use of tabs and spaces in indentation"," if a file mixes them in a way that's ambiguous, even if your editor renders it identically. Configure your editor to insert spaces only.",[31,1586,1587,1599,1600,1603,1604,1607,1608,1611,1612,1615],{},[23,1588,1589,1591,1592,1595,1596],{},[44,1590,1216],{}," changes ",[44,1593,1594],{},"sys.path[0]"," differently than ",[44,1597,1598],{},"python -m package.module"," — Running a file directly inserts the ",[127,1601,1602],{},"script's own directory"," at the front of ",[44,1605,1606],{},"sys.path","; running with ",[44,1609,1610],{},"-m"," inserts the ",[127,1613,1614],{},"current working directory"," instead. This difference is the root cause of many \"it works when I run it one way but not the other\" import bugs — covered in depth in chapter 17.",[14,1617,1619],{"id":1618},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[19,1621,1622,1623,1626],{},"A teammate says this script \"sometimes\" fails with ",[44,1624,1625],{},"ModuleNotFoundError"," depending on how they invoke it. Why?",[309,1628,1629],{"language":311},[313,1630,1632],{"className":315,"code":1631,"language":311,"meta":317,"style":317},"# project layout:\n# project\u002F\n#   src\u002F\n#     app\u002F\n#       __init__.py\n#       main.py      # does `from app.utils import helper`\n#       utils.py\n\ncd project\u002Fsrc\u002Fapp\npython main.py\n",[44,1633,1634,1639,1644,1649,1654,1659,1664,1669,1673,1680],{"__ignoreMap":317},[321,1635,1636],{"class":323,"line":324},[321,1637,1638],{"class":327},"# project layout:\n",[321,1640,1641],{"class":323,"line":331},[321,1642,1643],{"class":327},"# project\u002F\n",[321,1645,1646],{"class":323,"line":349},[321,1647,1648],{"class":327},"#   src\u002F\n",[321,1650,1651],{"class":323,"line":356},[321,1652,1653],{"class":327},"#     app\u002F\n",[321,1655,1656],{"class":323,"line":362},[321,1657,1658],{"class":327},"#       __init__.py\n",[321,1660,1661],{"class":323,"line":384},[321,1662,1663],{"class":327},"#       main.py      # does `from app.utils import helper`\n",[321,1665,1666],{"class":323,"line":408},[321,1667,1668],{"class":327},"#       utils.py\n",[321,1670,1671],{"class":323,"line":423},[321,1672,353],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":352},[321,1674,1675,1677],{"class":323,"line":428},[321,1676,494],{"class":411},[321,1678,1679],{"class":338}," project\u002Fsrc\u002Fapp\n",[321,1681,1682,1684],{"class":323,"line":434},[321,1683,524],{"class":334},[321,1685,1372],{"class":338},[1687,1688,1689,1693,1745],"details",{},[1690,1691,1692],"summary",{},"Answer",[19,1694,1695,1696,1699,1700,1703,1704,1706,1707,1710,1711,1713,1714,1717,1718,1721,1722,1721,1725,1727,1728,1730,1731,1734,1735,1737,1738,1740,1741,1744],{},"Running ",[44,1697,1698],{},"python main.py"," from inside ",[44,1701,1702],{},"app\u002F"," puts ",[44,1705,1702],{}," itself (not ",[44,1708,1709],{},"src\u002F",") at the front of ",[44,1712,1606],{},". So ",[44,1715,1716],{},"from app.utils import helper"," fails — Python is looking for a package named ",[44,1719,1720],{},"app"," ",[127,1723,1724],{},"inside",[44,1726,1702],{},", which doesn't exist. The fix is to run it as a module from the ",[44,1729,1709],{}," directory instead: ",[44,1732,1733],{},"cd project\u002Fsrc && python -m app.main",". This makes ",[44,1736,1709],{}," the path root, so ",[44,1739,1720],{}," resolves as the top-level package, and the internal ",[44,1742,1743],{},"app.utils"," import works correctly.",[19,1746,1747,1750,1751,1753,1754,1756],{},[23,1748,1749],{},"The lesson",": how you invoke a script determines what ",[44,1752,1594],{}," is, which determines whether internal absolute imports succeed — always run package-internal entry points with ",[44,1755,1610],{}," from the project root, not as a bare script from inside the package.",[14,1758,1760],{"id":1759},"key-takeaways","Key Takeaways",[28,1762,1763,1766,1775,1781,1784],{},[31,1764,1765],{},"Python is dynamically typed, multi-paradigm, and reference-counted with a cycle-collecting GC; CPython is the reference implementation you should default to.",[31,1767,1768,1769,1771,1772,1774],{},"Python source is compiled to bytecode (cached as ",[44,1770,50],{}," in ",[44,1773,1011],{},") and then interpreted by the CPython VM — it is neither purely interpreted nor ahead-of-time compiled.",[31,1776,1777,1778,1780],{},"Use ",[44,1779,170],{}," to manage Python versions per-project instead of relying on the system Python.",[31,1782,1783],{},"The REPL (or better, IPython) is a first-class tool for exploration, not just a toy.",[31,1785,1786,1787,982,1790,1793,1794,1796],{},"How you invoke a script (",[44,1788,1789],{},"python file.py",[44,1791,1792],{},"python -m pkg.module",") changes ",[44,1795,1606],{}," and can silently determine whether imports succeed.",[1798,1799,1800],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .snvgF, html code.shiki .snvgF{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-github-dark:#79B8FF}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}h